 "integration": {
  "summary": "Turn on Bus/Cloud control in the pump (HMI or Grundfos GO), then write 00101 bit 0 = 1 (RemoteAccessReq), choose the mode in 00105, write the setpoint (e.g. 00106-00107 in 0.1 ml/h) and send 00104 = 0 to start. Watch 00201 bit 0 to confirm remote control and poll 00204/00217/00218 for running, fault and warning.",
  "minimum_registers": [
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 100,
    "why": "Remote access request bit"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 103,
    "why": "Start/stop request"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 104,
    "why": "Operating mode"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 105,
    "why": "Manual dosing setpoint"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 200,
    "why": "Remote access confirmed"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 203,
    "why": "Running / warning / fault bits"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 216,
    "why": "Fault code"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 217,
    "why": "Warning code"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 305,
    "why": "Measured dosing capacity"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 311,
    "why": "Total dosed volume"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "In the pump HMI or the Grundfos GO app set Settings > Communication > Bus/Cloud control = On. Then set 00101 bit 0 (RemoteAccessReq) = 1; without it all control bits are ignored. Relays and the analog output answer Modbus only when their function is set to Bus control in the pump.",
  "watchdog": "A fixed 10 s communication watchdog is switched on the first time Bus/Cloud control is enabled; it can be turned off or on with 00102 bit 2 (persistent). If Modbus traffic stops for more than 10 s the pump stops dosing and raises alarm 15; it resumes when communication returns.",
  "quirks": [
   "Register numbers are 1-based: 00101 goes out as address 100.",
   "Commands in 00103 act on a rising edge; with AutoAckControlBits (00005) = 0 you must write the bit back to 0 before the next command.",
   "ReqStop cannot stop the pump while it is de-aerating."
  ],
  "setup": [
   "DDA model C (SoftCIM RTU): in Grundfos GO, Settings > Communication > RS485 AYB: protocol Modbus RTU, address 1-247, 9600/19200/38400 baud, parity and stop bits; the M12 port needs a termination plug at the line end.",
   "DDA model C (SoftCIM TCP): Settings > Communication > Ethernet RJ45: Ethernet On, protocol Modbus TCP, DHCP or static IP, TCP port (default 502).",
   "CIM 200: the slave address is set in the pump menu (its hex rotary switches are not used with DDA). SW4/SW5 select 9600 (OFF/ON), 19200 (OFF/OFF, default), 38400 (ON/OFF) or software-defined (ON/ON); SW3 OFF = even parity 1 stop, ON = no parity 2 stop; SW1+SW2 ON = 150 ohm termination in.",
   "CIM 500: set the rotary switch to Modbus TCP and set the IP in its web server (default 192.168.1.100, user admin); the Modbus TCP IP must differ from the web server IP."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "If Bus/Cloud control is not enabled in the pump, 00201 bit 0 stays 0 and no write takes effect.",
   "With Bus/Cloud control on, settings can no longer be changed from the pump HMI or GO app.",
   "Measured capacity and pressure read nothing useful unless FlowControl (00102 bit 1) is enabled."
  ]
 },
